<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>

  <!-- ====================================================================
       FIX: More Realistic Research broken cross-reference

       Startup log error:
         Could not resolve cross-reference: No Verse.ResearchProjectDef
         named SecurityDoor found to give to
         ResearchMakesSense.ManualAnalysisDef 9

       More Realistic Research ships a ManualAnalysisDef (defName "9")
       targeting a research project called SecurityDoor. No such
       ResearchProjectDef exists in this load order - the only SecurityDoor
       in the game is a ThingDef from VFE Medieval 2, not a research
       project. The reference is stale, pointing at a mod we do not run.

       Removing the orphaned def is correct. Adding a stub ResearchProjectDef
       to satisfy the reference would put a phantom entry in the research
       tree, which is worse.

       success = Always because the mod's About.xml <name> has a trailing
       space ("More Realistic Research "), which makes PatchOperationFindMod
       unreliable here. If the author ever fixes the reference upstream, this
       operation simply finds nothing and does nothing.
       ==================================================================== -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationRemove">
    <xpath>/Defs/ResearchMakesSense.ManualAnalysisDef[researchProject="SecurityDoor"]</xpath>
    <success>Always</success>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
